[Seedance 2.5 — production reference (ByteDance, official guides of 2026-07-31) › 4. Syntax markers for audio, dialogue and text] Dialogue language reinforcement — the formula is `Dialogue language + regional variety or accent + delivery style + speaker + {line}`:
Dialogue language: authentic Los Angeles English. The young man says in natural
Los Angeles vernacular: {No way, you actually made it.}
The girl says softly in Japanese: {もう大丈夫です}

[Seedance 2.5 — production reference (ByteDance, official guides of 2026-07-31) › 5. Reference discipline (the 50-slot system)] Role template:
@Image 1 defines <subject>'s <appearance, clothing, structure, or material>.
@Video 1 defines <motion, camera movement, or pacing>.
@Audio 1 defines <character or sound type>'s <voice, dialogue, ambience, or music>.
